#: ../../source/generated/modules/freeports_dev.ci.formats.rst:2
msgid "freeports\\_dev.ci.formats"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.formats:1 of
msgid ""
"``freeports-dev coverage`` for a formats repository: how much of it is "
"actually tested."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.formats:3 of
msgid ""
"Two figures, both over the same unit — the **document**, which is a "
"format holding one ``report.pdf`` or one subdirectory of a format holding"
" several:"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.formats:6 of
msgid ""
"``tests.formats.integration`` — documents whose whole-document test "
"exists at all, which is to say documents with an ``out/`` for the run to "
"be checked against;"
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.formats:8 of
msgid ""
"``tests.formats.single_page`` — documents carrying at least one page with"
" the whole fixture triple, so that every stage of the pipeline is pinned "
"somewhere in that document."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.formats:11 of
#, python-format
msgid ""
"They answer different questions and a repository can be strong in one and"
" weak in the other, which is exactly why they are two thresholds and not "
"an average. A repository at 100 % single-page and 86 % integration — "
"which is this workspace's formats repository today — has every format's "
"stages pinned page by page and five documents nobody has ever run end to "
"end. One number would hide that."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.formats:16 of
msgid ""
"The walk is :mod:`freeports_dev.format_inventory`, shared with the pytest"
" plugin so that the report cannot claim a coverage the suite does not "
"collect. It reads file names and nothing else: no PDF is opened, no "
"algorithm is loaded, so this is a **fast** metric and belongs in the "
"commit hook."
msgstr ""

