msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.formats.FormatsCoverage.measurements:1 of
msgid "Both metrics, in the normalised shape the gate reads."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.formats.FormatsCoverage.missing_integration:1 of
msgid "The documents holding the integration figure down, by name, in order."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.formats.FormatsCoverage.missing_integration:3 of
msgid ""
"Named rather than counted because a percentage is what a threshold "
"compares and a list of names is what somebody acts on. Every rendering "
"prints both."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.formats.FormatsCoverage.problems:1 of
msgid "Malformed documents, as ``(name, message)``, from the same walk."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.formats.FormatsCoverage.problems:3 of
msgid ""
"A repository with one broken document is still measured and the breakage "
"is named. A report that refuses to print because one document is "
"malformed tells you less than one that prints and says which."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.formats.FormatsCoverage.ratio:1 of
msgid ""
"A percentage, with an empty repository reading 100 rather than dividing "
"by zero."
msgstr ""

#: freeports_dev.ci.formats.FormatsCoverage.ratio:3 of
msgid ""
"An empty repository has no untested document in it. Calling that 0 % "
"would refuse the first commit to a repository that has nothing wrong with"
" it, which is how a gate teaches people to turn it off."
msgstr ""

